---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import QualificationNotice from "../components/QualificationNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Verification | BeaconGuard Verify"
  description="BeaconGuard Verify is a read-only investigation surface for executive reporting, Decision Explorer, deterministic reconstruction, source evidence, replay verification, verifiable export, and non-authoritative AI-assisted insights."
  pageClass="page-verification"
>
  <section class="verification-hero">
    <div class="verification-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">BEACONGUARD VERIFY</p>

      <h1>Investigate decisions without changing authority.</h1>

      <p class="verification-hero-lead">
        BeaconGuard Verify gives security, privacy, compliance, risk, and audit
        reviewers a read-only surface for inspecting governed AI transaction
        evidence without granting runtime permission.
      </p>

      <div class="page-actions verification-hero-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/proof-evidence">Inspect Proof and Evidence</a>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/sample-decision-record"
          >View Sample Decision Record</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="verification-hero-diagram">
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/verification/beaconguard-evidence-centered-investigation.png"
        alt="Evidence-centered investigation architecture. Request Admission and Result-to-Action decisions produce canonical evidence. BeaconGuard Verify provides a read-only boundary for decision exploration, deterministic reconstruction, source-evidence review, replay verification, executive reporting, and verifiable export. AI-assisted insights remain separate, non-authoritative, and outside the trusted reconstruction and runtime authorization paths."
        width="1672"
        height="941"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band" aria-labelledby="verify-boundary-heading">
    <h2 id="verify-boundary-heading">The read-only verification boundary</h2>
    <p class="verify-band-lead">
      BeaconGuard Verify inspects recorded authorization evidence after the
      decision. It cannot modify evidence, change a historical outcome, activate
      a release, alter a Compliance Playbook, grant runtime authority, or
      authorize an enterprise action.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band" aria-labelledby="verify-capabilities-heading">
    <h2 id="verify-capabilities-heading">Investigation capabilities</h2>
    <div class="verify-capability-grid">
      <div class="verify-capability-group">
        <h3 class="verify-capability-group-title">Investigate</h3>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Decision Explorer</h4>
          <p>
            Search and inspect recorded authorization decisions and their linked
            transaction context.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Executive Reporting</h4>
          <p>
            Summarize investigation-relevant decision evidence for review and
            oversight without granting runtime authority.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="verify-capability-group">
        <h3 class="verify-capability-group-title">Reconstruct and verify</h3>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Deterministic Reconstruction</h4>
          <p>
            Rebuild the recorded decision path from canonical evidence without
            inventing missing fields or model reasoning.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Source Evidence</h4>
          <p>
            Trace reconstructed fields to referenced artifacts, digests,
            integrity status, and recorded provenance.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Replay Verification</h4>
          <p>
            Check a recorded decision against its governing artifacts as an
            investigation operation, not as a substitute for live runtime
            enforcement.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="verify-capability-group">
        <h3 class="verify-capability-group-title">Package and interpret</h3>
        <article class="verify-capability-card">
          <h4>Verifiable Export</h4>
          <p>
            Produce an integrity-checkable investigation package for review.
            Export does not establish legal admissibility.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article
          class="verify-capability-card verify-capability-card--non-authoritative"
        >
          <p class="verify-non-auth-label">Non-authoritative</p>
          <h4>AI-Assisted Insights</h4>
          <p>
            Help reviewers navigate or summarize evidence while remaining
            non-authoritative and outside the trusted reconstruction and runtime
            authorization paths.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band" aria-labelledby="verify-provenance-heading">
    <h2 id="verify-provenance-heading">Evidence provenance and reconstruction</h2>
    <ul class="verify-provenance-list">
      <li>
        Authorization decisions produce Verifiable Decision Records that preserve
        decision context and related identifiers.
      </li>
      <li>
        Release and playbook identities support reconstruction of the governing
        configuration used at decision time.
      </li>
      <li>
        Request and action correlation links the transaction stages for
        investigation.
      </li>
      <li>
        Trust, freshness, and replay results are preserved where configured.
      </li>
      <li>
        Source-evidence references support field-level traceability to artifacts
        and digests.
      </li>
      <li>
        Missing or unavailable evidence must remain visible rather than being
        invented.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band" aria-labelledby="verify-cannot-heading">
    <h2 id="verify-cannot-heading">What Verify cannot do</h2>
    <ul class="bg-nonclaim-list">
      <li>Modify or delete historical evidence.</li>
      <li>Convert DENY into ALLOW.</li>
      <li>Activate or replace an Active Verified Release.</li>
      <li>Alter a Compliance Playbook.</li>
      <li>Grant runtime authority.</li>
      <li>Authorize an enterprise action.</li>
      <li>Treat AI-assisted insight as evidence authority.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band" aria-labelledby="verify-responsibility-heading">
    <h2 id="verify-responsibility-heading">Responsibility separation</h2>
    <div class="verify-responsibility-grid">
      <div class="verify-responsibility-card">
        <h3>BeaconGuard</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Records and exposes authorization evidence.</li>
          <li>Provides read-only investigation capabilities.</li>
          <li>Does not execute enterprise actions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="verify-responsibility-card">
        <h3>Enterprise application</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Declares and executes authorized actions.</li>
          <li>Correlates decisions with workflow context.</li>
          <li>Enforces DENY and non-AI fallback behavior.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="verify-responsibility-card">
        <h3>Enterprise systems of record</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Remain authoritative for resulting business state.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="verify-responsibility-card">
        <h3>Customer governance</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Retains legal, clinical, operational, compliance, and business
            judgment.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band verify-band--qualify">
    <QualificationNotice variant="full" />
  </section>

  <section class="verify-band verify-band--cta" aria-label="Next steps">
    <div class="page-actions verification-final-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/proof-evidence">Inspect Proof and Evidence</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/reviewer-kit">Open Reviewer Kit</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
